{% /* ==========================================================================
      dps abandoned cart, JSON.  Content > Dynamic Content > New > JSON.

      The same basket as abandoned-cart.html, as data rather than markup. A push
      carousel reads it through "Get from Dynamic Content", and anything else that
      wants the products without a layout can use it too.

      ONE ASSET PER SCENARIO, THREE RENDERINGS. The query below is identical to the
      HTML one on purpose: a second copy of the query would be a second thing to keep
      correct, and the failure would be a push and an email disagreeing about what is
      in somebody's basket.

      COMMAS ARE THE WHOLE DIFFICULTY IN A JSON TEMPLATE. A loop that writes a comma
      after every item produces a trailing one and invalid JSON, which Dengage rejects
      on save. So the comma is written BEFORE every item except the first, tracked with
      a counter rather than the loop index, because skipped rows would leave gaps.
      ====================================================================== */ %}
{% var lines = $from("shopping_cart_events")
     .where("contact_key", "=", $Contact.contact_key)
     .orderByDescending("event_date")
     .take(3)
     .get(); %}
{% var written = 0; %}
{"items":[
{% for (var i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) { %}
  {% var p = $from("dps_product")
       .where("product_id", "=", lines[i].product_id)
       .take(1)
       .get()[0]; %}
  {% if (p && p.is_active == 1) { %}
    {% if (written > 0) { %},{% } %}
    {"id":"{%= p.product_id =%}",
     "title":"{%= p.title =%}",
     "category":"{%= p.category_path =%}",
     "price":"{%= p.discounted_price || p.price =%}",
     "was":"{%= p.discounted_price ? p.price : '' =%}",
     "image":"{%= p.image_link =%}",
     "link":"{%= p.mobile_web_link || p.link =%}",
     "quantity":"{%= lines[i].quantity =%}"}
    {% written = written + 1; %}
  {% } %}
{% } %}
],"count":"{%= written =%}"}
